From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:14:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08047/11362] The stall induction's two induce calls are
 different call sites, and only one carries the gates

Phase 1 (best-of-N) capture. Building it corrected an assumption the confirm phase had left
implicit, and the correction changes which prompt is worth measuring.

`_induce_and_plan` issues TWO induce calls inside ONE stall attempt, and they are not retries of
each other. Stack capture (not inference): call 1 comes from `execute_bounded_llm_reinduction`
(arc_competition_agent.py:5770, the stall branch); call 2 comes from the plain single-shot path
120 lines further down the same function (:5889). The confirm phase measured call 2 by default.
All three gates the criteria name -- held-out verifier, goal gate, plan_in_model -- live on call
1 and run there by default, while the plain path's goal check is opt-in and DEFAULT OFF
(`CARNOT_ARC_PLAIN_PATH_GOAL_SATISFIABILITY_CHECK`), so grading criterion (ii) at call 2 would
grade a gate the live agent does not run.

Call 1's split is also the better evidence, and by a margin that matters. `_proposal_prefix` is
applied there, so `full` is the real 25-row set and the live suffix survives into the held-out
side; at call 2 full == prefix and the suffix is unrecoverable. Measured consequence, from
split.py's own proof run: ft09 goes from 0 held-out CHANGING rows at call 2 to 4 at call 1.
Zero changing rows means an identity engine scores a perfect held-out accuracy, so that game was
unscoreable for change quality and is now scoreable. tu93 19, tn36 17, sc25 1, lp85 still 0.

`root_grid` is newly captured, and criteria (ii)/(iii) are impossible without it. Both gates are
searches rooted at `E3AgentPolicy.root_grid`, which is handed to `execute_bounded_llm_reinduction`
as a keyword and never reaches the proposer -- so capture_p3's proposer-side recorder could not
see it. The wrapper goes on the name BOUND IN `arc_competition_agent`, because that module does a
from-import at load time and patching the definition in `arc_llm_reinduction` would be a no-op.

The six games split into five STALL inductions and one post-bank, and the split is MEASURED
rather than asserted: ft09/lp85/sc25/tn36/tu93 all report levels_gained 0 with 25 collected
transitions, and vc33 reports levels_gained 2 with ONE transition and ZERO held-out rows. vc33 is
exactly the vacuity trap this phase was warned about -- a criterion scored there passes
near-trivially -- so it is partitioned out of the headline and kept as the contrast rather than
dropped silently.

What is NOT here yet: the candidates and their scores. Generation is live and its output lands in
the next commit. The scorer is committed now because it is what defines the criteria, and it
should be readable before any number it produces exists.

